($t$Apocynum cannabinum$t$, $t$Apocynum cannabinum$t$, $t$Apocynaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Apocynaceae. Portamento: Perennial. Altezza massima indicativa: 0.6 m. A perennial herbaceous plant with some edible, medicinal and other uses. A very good quality fibre obtained from the bark is used for making clothes, twine, bags, linen, and paper. Indian hemp is an unpleasantly bitter stimulant irritant herb that acts on the heart, respiratory and urinary systems, and also on the uterus. It has been used as a Antirheumatic;  Cardiotonic;  Diaphoretic;  Diuretic;  Emetic;  Expectorant;  Tonic;  VD;   Vermifuge;  and for Warts. Similar to Cannabis (Cannabis sativa) as a fiber plant (see Hemp) but not  as a source of a psychoactive drug. Common names include: Dogbane, Amy Root, Hemp Dogbane, Prairie Dogbane, Indian Hemp, Rheumatism Root, or Wild Cotton. Can be misspelt as Apocynum cannibinum$t$, $j${"luce": "Tollera: pieno sole, mezz'ombra, ombra", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Indian Hemp$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): All parts of the plant are poisonous[1, 4, 19, 62]. It contains toxic cardioactive glycosides[222].$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Apocynaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "fin